#: ../../source/docs/follow-mode.rst:5 93ddbccad8b84fa2be517c686b1ed597
msgid "Follow Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/follow-mode.rst:10 56f1c061b7504b4093bb50aa4585ae30
msgid ""
"When switched into Follow, the vehicle will attempt to follow another "
"vehicle (or anything publishing its position) at a specified offset.  The"
" vehicle lead vehicle's position must be published to the vehicle in "
"Follow mode using a telemetry system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/follow-mode.rst:12 43385c8e7d7d4b65a4548565118586ff
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The altitude is maintained with the altitude hold controller so the "
"vehicle will attempt to hold its current altitude when the sticks are "
"placed with 10% of mid-throttle. It will climb or descend at up to 2.5m/s"
" (this speed is adjustable with the :ref:`PILOT_SPEED_UP<PILOT_SPEED_UP>`"
" and :ref:`PILOT_SPEED_DN<PILOT_SPEED_DN>` parameters). The acceleration "
"used to establish these speeds is set by "
":ref:`PILOT_ACCEL_Z<PILOT_ACCEL_Z>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/follow-mode.rst:14 cedd19c5709247bd89553bb67583f0d3
msgid "The following parameters can be used to tune Follow Mode's performance:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/follow-mode.rst:16 6813e8be33424a1e83f5421459e78838
msgid ""
":ref:`FOLL_ENABLE <FOLL_ENABLE>`: set to 1 to enable follow mode and "
"refresh parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/follow-mode.rst:17 b98faf856ad841e0af548c1d324166eb
msgid ""
":ref:`FOLL_SYSID <FOLL_SYSID>`: MAVLink system id of lead vehicle (\"0\" "
"means follow the first vehicle \"seen\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/follow-mode.rst:18 87884c0dd7234b5bab9049b594683c14
msgid ""
":ref:`FOLL_DIST_MAX <FOLL_DIST_MAX>`: if lead vehicle is more than this "
"many meters away, give up on following and hold position"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/follow-mode.rst:19 62983c78d3d04fe2ba6a678e1e0576b0
msgid ""
":ref:`FOLL_OFS_X <FOLL_OFS_X>`, :ref:`FOLL_OFS_Y <FOLL_OFS_Y>`, "
":ref:`FOLL_OFS_Z <FOLL_OFS_Z>`: 3D offset (in meters) from the lead "
"vehicle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/follow-mode.rst:20 e49e448fdbbd4f87b37277543257a199
msgid ""
":ref:`FOLL_OFS_TYPE <FOLL_OFS_TYPE>`: set to 0 if offsets are North-East-"
"Down, 1 if offsets are relative to lead vehicle's heading"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/follow-mode.rst:21 949ac75586b645139ec6f28dcfbe514f
msgid ""
":ref:`FOLL_YAW_BEHAVE <FOLL_YAW_BEHAVE>`: controls whether follow points "
"in the same direction as lead vehicle or always towards it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/follow-mode.rst:22 d0ebb00f539546cd951f3056fc0ed0bf
msgid ""
":ref:`FOLL_POS_P <FOLL_POS_P>`: gain which controls how aggressively this"
" vehicle moves towards lead vehicle (limited by :ref:`WPNAV_SPEED "
"<WPNAV_SPEED>`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/follow-mode.rst:23 a5f500298f474a72b5b310aff1338f57
msgid ""
":ref:`FOLL_ALT_TYPE <FOLL_ALT_TYPE>`: allows selecting whether to use "
"lead vehicle's relative-to-home or relative-to-sea-level altitude"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/follow-mode.rst:24 94d9ce1c34994213a5dff5f49b948945
msgid ""
":ref:`FOLL_OPTIONS<FOLL_OPTIONS>`: set bit 0 to \"1\" to enable the :ref"
":`common-mount-targeting` to follow the target vehicle."
msgstr ""

